WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.435
-You know our first guest
tonight from films like

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.338
"300" and the
"Olympus has Fallen" franchise.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.706
He stars in
and produced "Plane,"

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.707
which is in theaters Friday.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.808
Let's take a look.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.509
-If I didn't believe it
could be done,

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:12.879
I would not put you guys
back on that plane.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.383
I have a daughter.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.884
I have every intention of
hugging her again

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:20.186
and making it home.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:24.758
And I'm telling you that the way
home is on this plane.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.092
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.227
our friend Gerard Butler,
everybody!

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:30.630
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.747
Welcome back!
It's been a while.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.749
-Where have you been in my life?
-I know.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.017
I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.152
I want to start --
First of all, happy new year.

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:54.787
I know it's a couple weeks ago,

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.589
but, you know, you're
an international movie star.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.391
I feel like you have a wealth of
options on New Year's Eve.

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:02.562
And you were --
You spent it in Times Square.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.597
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.199
-Yeah, well, now you put it
like that, it's pretty sad.

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:08.334
-You should have put it
like that,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.536
like, you know, December 21st

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:11.870
and more like,
"What am I doing?"

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.973
-No, my friends wanted to go.
I swear it wasn't me.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.041
-Okay.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.176
-And I didn't want to be
a party pooper.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:19.011
But we're also friends with
Duran Duran,

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:20.146
so we thought, "Well,
that would be kind of fun."

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.547
-Alright.
Seeing Duran Duran live.

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:23.516
Now it makes sense.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.418
-But it didn't really go
according to plan...

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.752
-Okay.

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:30.056
-...because we -- Well, firstly,
we arrive in this room,

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.258
which seemed to be
the guests of Duran Duran.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.894
And -- But when we finally go to
go to the stage --

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.129
and it's maybe just before 11:00
at this point --

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.699
we get this --
It was almost a 25-minute walk.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:42.868
I'm not jo-- We go through
hotels and around avenues

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.138
and through blockades
and then other hotels.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.240
And then we finally
get to this place,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.008
and it said, "Disney party."

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.576
So everybody is
looking at us like,

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:51.944
"What are you guys doing here?"

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:54.414
So we go, "Okay, well,
the stage must be outside."

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.348
So we walk outside,
and there is these two barriers.

00:01:56.348 --> 00:01:58.484
There's like
half-a-million people this side,

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:01.153
half-a-million people that side,
and just us.

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.989
Five of us on our own with
everybody now screaming at us.

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:06.291
I thought maybe I'm supposed to
do a performance or something.

00:02:06.291 --> 00:02:08.294
So, we say to somebody,
"Well, where is the stage?"

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.828
And they're like,
"Oh, no, the stage is like

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:11.331
five blocks that way."

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:12.565
And we can't even see the stage.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.033
So now we're
running desperately.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.102
And everybody is trying to pull
us back into this party, saying,

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.603
"Will you take a photo
with so-and-so?"

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:18.671
and blah, blah, blah.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.506
And we're begging.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:23.642
We can't even get into
the main throng of the crowd.

00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:26.012
So -- And the police --
they all want photos.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.280
But then we say,
"Can we go through?"

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.215
And they go,
"No, no, you can't go through."

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.617
-So these are police officers
that want a picture with you,

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:32.885
but then will not
let you through.

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:35.455
-And then say, "Nobody can go
through this way."

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.156
And then I'm getting stopped
by everybody,

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:39.358
so I end up putting on
one of those ridiculous hats.

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:40.793
So I am running around
with this going,

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.296
"But what if somebody
photographs me and I look..."

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.430
-I like that somebody
would be like,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.798
"I think that's Gerard Butler."

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.832
And they'd would be like, "No,

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.201
he would never wear
a hat that dumb."

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:51.371
-Exactly. That was the argument
that my friends used.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:54.474
And then, at one point,
it was now about 11:30.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.775
And we have been 20 minutes
by these

00:02:56.775 --> 00:02:58.811
20 port-a-potties
in the pissing rain

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.045
and thought, "This is it.

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:02.181
This is how we are
going spend our New Year --

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.449
by the port-a-potties.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.884
And we don't even know which
part -- where we're at."

00:03:05.884 --> 00:03:08.321
And then, finally,
we found the greeter.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:11.357
And they took us just as
Duran Duran were coming on.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.625
And we were at this barrier.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.960
And they -- As Simon Le Bon
walks up the stage,

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:15.961
they open the barrier.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.430
Suddenly, we run up the stairs.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.532
And we're right there
3 feet from the stage.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.201
It's a quarter to midnight.
The ball drops.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:23.602
Confetti everywhere.
-So, in the end, it worked.

00:03:23.602 --> 00:03:24.904
-So in the end, it worked.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:28.508
But I say I've ticked that one
off my bucket list.

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:31.009
I think I'm good with
Times Square.

00:03:31.009 --> 00:03:32.111
I think I'm good with
Times Square generally.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.546
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.482
It's not like it rises to the
occasion on the other days.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.551
Yeah.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:42.722
So, this is fantastic.
This is an action movie.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.858
I think the kind of fun that
we expect from you in a film.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:48.460
And I will say,
I really love the title "Plane."

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:52.498
I like that it's just
coming right in.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:55.234
It's telling you what to expect.
I got to admit, though.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.370
I think sometimes maybe
movie studios

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.471
would overthink this
and come up with

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:02.041
something more complicated
than "Plane."

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.709
-I couldn't agree more.

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:06.245
I have to say, in its defense,
at one point,

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.114
it was changed to "The Plane."

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.181
-Okay.

00:04:09.181 --> 00:04:11.717
-But --
-Huge mistake.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.152
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.519
When we were filming,
suddenly, on the script,

00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:15.554
it said, "The Plane."

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.222
But look at "Flight."

00:04:17.222 --> 00:04:19.291
You know, and this is
a classic action movie.

00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:21.293
I mean, it is really
a throwback to those --

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:22.862
And I think we have them
less and less.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.431
The old superhero,
"Star Wars" -- they're great,

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:28.567
but I miss those movies where
you have the John McClane,

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.703
you know, the Bruce Willis,
the Harrison Ford.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:35.274
And, you know, so, I actually
think a title like that

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.410
really allows you to feel --
you know, feel into it.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.178
You can kind of make your own
decisions on it.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:41.079
And it actually
is not all on a plane.

00:04:41.079 --> 00:04:43.515
It's very plane-centric,
but that's only the start of it

00:04:43.515 --> 00:04:46.318
after this kind of
really quite --

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:48.454
-Yeah. You're on an island.
-Yeah.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.455
-So you could have
called it "Island."

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.791
-"Plane and Island," yeah, yeah.

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:56.395
-Like halfway through,
you should have just turned,

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:58.798
broke the fourth wall,
turned to the camera, and gone,

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.234
"The movie is
called 'Island' now."

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:06.038
-I'm out of here. Okay.
-No!

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:08.708
No, I like talking --
I mean, you are --

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:09.976
Ever since the first time
I met you,

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:12.044
you've always been in
these films where I feel

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.313
like you put yourself
at great physical risk.

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:16.915
And, yet -- There is all these
stunts, all this action,

00:05:16.915 --> 00:05:18.684
but I have heard
that you hurt yourself

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:23.989
more on this film pretending --
just pretending to fix a plane.

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:27.192
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:27.192 --> 00:05:28.627
-So, what happened?

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:30.530
-Yeah, I think I managed to --

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.332
No matter what I'm doing,
I manage to hurt myself.

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.067
-Are you naturally clumsy?

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.668
-I think so, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.668 --> 00:05:40.439
-But it was on the scene where
you just saw the clip.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:44.843
We -- I'm trying to
find something

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:46.845
that's wrong with the plane
before we can take off

00:05:46.845 --> 00:05:47.980
for this final sequence.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.783
And it's something in the wheel,
so it's a brake.

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:53.218
Now I'm sticking my hand
between these two wheels,

00:05:53.218 --> 00:05:55.588
kind of pretending
that I know what I'm doing.

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:58.391
And it's so --
Whatever is in there is, like --

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.892
Every time I bring my hands out,

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:02.995
they're covered in blood
and green fluid, right?

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.797
And I'm like -- I don't know
what this green fluid is.

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.231
We're also shooting in
Puerto Rico,

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:07.933
so I'm covered in sweat.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:09.202
And the adrenaline.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:10.736
And the nose
is running, everything.

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:13.673
And I guess especially
with COVID,

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:16.075
you realize why
this thing spreads, right?

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:19.145
Because I must have been --
I'm rubbing my face.

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:22.748
And, suddenly,
it's in my throat.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.450
It's in my mouth.
It's up my nose.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.618
It's in my eyes.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:28.053
It's burning my face,
and I mean burning.

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:31.023
It turns out this is essentially
phosphoric acid.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:34.961
And the airline pilots that were
there watching go, "No!"

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.562
They're trying to
put water on my face.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:39.498
"Don't put water.
It will make it worse!"

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:40.833
And I'm just,
like, burning alive.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.234
So it was intense.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.969
And it actually burned
for hours,

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:46.171
but it was great for
the sequence.

00:06:46.171 --> 00:06:48.574
-And anything for the work.
Anything for the work.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.309
-Anything for the work, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:54.947
-I like -- Knowing everything
I know about COVID protocols

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.516
these days on movie sets,
there were probably

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.951
10 people there making sure
nobody gave each other COVID,

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:03.088
and not one person keeping you
from putting acid on your face.

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:04.557
-Yeah, that's pretty much it.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:07.393
-Now this, though, I really --
This is a true credit to you.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.962
And I can't believe --
And I also want to say

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.097
I'm crediting you that you never
told me this story before.

00:07:12.097 --> 00:07:15.367
You actually, real life,
saved a human being.

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:18.070
This is not movie.
This is not character work.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.539
You fished someone from a river.

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:22.375
-Yeah. I've saved a couple of
human beings,

00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:25.378
but this one --
[ Laughs ]

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:27.246
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Save it for next time.

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:30.749
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.
-Save one for next time.

00:07:30.749 --> 00:07:32.618
-Yeah, actually,
when I just started acting,

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:36.521
I -- The place that I filmed my
first movie,

00:07:36.521 --> 00:07:37.790
it was a beautiful place,

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.692
but with this River Tay
in Scotland.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.994
But it is cold and it has
a lot of undercurrent.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.162
But it was a beautiful
summer's day.

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:44.963
And I say to my mom,
"Let's go where I stayed.

00:07:44.963 --> 00:07:46.332
This is the hotel I stayed at."

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:48.401
And we're both just lying there,
and we fall asleep.

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:50.769
And, suddenly,
I hear this screaming.

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:52.238
And I wake up.

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:54.306
I say to the woman next to me,
"Is there somebody in trouble?

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:55.508
She goes, "Uh, I don't know."

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.576
And nobody seems
to take notice of this.

00:07:57.576 --> 00:07:59.612
And, so, I go over this hill.

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:02.181
And, sure enough, there is this
boy in the middle of the river.

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.816
And he disappears underwater
and then he comes back up.

00:08:04.816 --> 00:08:06.619
And then he just --
And he looks dead to me.

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:11.457
And all I could think was, "I
wish I was a heavier sleeper."

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:13.192
'Cause I'm like, "What am I --

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.027
You know, I know
I'm going to go in there,

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.561
but I just wish
I hadn't woken up."

00:08:16.561 --> 00:08:17.563
And I did.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:18.998
But, so, this part of the --

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.734
Yeah, I've got courage,
but clumsy as hell.

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.936
I did probably
the worst rescue attempt.

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.771
So, I swim out
and then I grab him.

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:28.874
But I didn't go back, so I was
kind of, like, you know --

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:30.810
-Yeah. Holding his
head underwater?

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.478
-Yeah, yeah.

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.680
And the kid was basically --

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.014
You know,
his eyes were wide open.

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:38.718
And we get him back.
-How old was he when you saved?

00:08:38.718 --> 00:08:40.119
-He was 13.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:41.887
-And we get back,
and now I'm just holding him.

00:08:41.887 --> 00:08:43.355
And he's lying there.

00:08:43.355 --> 00:08:45.291
And I think if we had been left
to that, he would have died,

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:46.392
'cause I didn't know what to do.

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:47.627
-He probably
was looking up being like,

00:08:47.627 --> 00:08:50.596
"Oh, anybody but Gerard Butler."

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:52.498
-Well, especially in
the position we were in.

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:53.999
-Yeah.

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:55.634
-That's another one.

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:59.905
So -- And this guy came over and
gave him the Heimlich maneuver,

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:02.274
and he threw up
and then he, you know, came to.

00:09:02.274 --> 00:09:04.610
And then he was fine.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.146
And, actually,
I got an award for bravery

00:09:07.146 --> 00:09:08.581
from the British Humane Society
for that.

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:09.849
-There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:12.852
Now, this is really special.

00:09:12.852 --> 00:09:15.487
You -- I mean, you stay in touch
with him over the years.

00:09:15.487 --> 00:09:16.622
He is 13 at the time.
-I did.

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:19.558
-And he got married recently,

00:09:19.558 --> 00:09:21.694
and his best man
reached out to you

00:09:21.694 --> 00:09:23.562
and asked if you would make
a video for his wedding,

00:09:23.562 --> 00:09:25.831
which I assume
you took this seriously.

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:27.266
-Oh, yeah, I did. I did.

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:29.301
This is why I ended up
producing movies,

00:09:29.301 --> 00:09:31.804
because I'm such a perfectionist
that I didn't just --

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:34.540
I think I spent a whole day
putting this together,

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.608
'cause I thought,
"I got to do a good job here.

00:09:36.608 --> 00:09:38.243
They're going to show it
for their wedding."

00:09:38.243 --> 00:09:40.979
So I think I recorded four,
and it took like six hours.

00:09:40.979 --> 00:09:43.783
And I'm like, "What am I doing?
This is ridiculous!"

00:09:43.783 --> 00:09:45.484
You know, but it was actually --

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:48.186
Because he wrote me a letter
after that, when he was 13,

00:09:48.186 --> 00:09:49.321
and it was very sweet.

00:09:49.321 --> 00:09:51.590
And, suddenly, to feel --
The best man

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:52.924
had got in touch, saying,

00:09:52.924 --> 00:09:55.093
"It would be so amazing if you
did this speech for him."

00:09:55.093 --> 00:09:57.096
You know, obviously, my career
had changed a little bit,

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:58.864
so they would actually
know who I was then.

00:09:58.864 --> 00:10:01.867
And, so, yeah,
I recorded this speech.

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:03.502
-And you were kind enough
to bring it with you.

00:10:03.502 --> 00:10:06.271
So this is the video
that played at the wedding.

00:10:06.271 --> 00:10:08.774
-Hey, Danny. Hey, Nicola.

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:11.310
Uh, congratulations.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.612
Danny, I haven't seen you
for a while --

00:10:13.612 --> 00:10:15.981
since you were about 13.

00:10:15.981 --> 00:10:21.120
We lost you on the River Tay in
Scotland, and I pulled you out,

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:25.724
and there you are today
getting married.

00:10:25.724 --> 00:10:28.160
So it's kind of a cool moment.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.765
I have to say, I was quite moved
when I heard this,

00:10:32.765 --> 00:10:36.602
because you're responsible
for me getting an award from

00:10:36.602 --> 00:10:38.236
the British Humane Society.

00:10:38.236 --> 00:10:40.739
And, you know, for the
older aunts and uncles,

00:10:40.739 --> 00:10:42.040
close your ears.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.743
But you have no idea how often
that's got me laid.

00:10:44.743 --> 00:10:46.411
[ Laughter ]

00:10:46.411 --> 00:10:48.114
But I'm asking for
nothing from you guys

00:10:48.114 --> 00:10:51.183
except maybe to name
your firstborn Gerry,

00:10:51.183 --> 00:10:54.053
boy or girl -- or, you know,
all your kids Gerry.

00:10:54.053 --> 00:10:59.324
-[ Laughs ] Bravo!

00:10:59.324 --> 00:11:03.729
Gerard Butler, everybody,
Humane Society Award winner!

00:11:03.729 --> 00:11:05.497
"Plane" is in theaters Friday.

00:11:05.497 --> 00:11:07.900
We'll be right back with
Nico Parker.

